  "scope": "The candidate copies the unchanged production custody, reservation and no-replace logic. It registers a named non-default VFS only for the tested queue connection and records successful natural page-zero maps. Missing or changed identities refuse the operation. A single-connection worker owns the map lifetime.",
  "arms": {
    "scan": "Same test VFS and checks; reads all of /proc/self/maps on each check to match the natural address. This is an instrumented full-scan reference, not a shipping app benchmark.",
    "address": "A fixed 104-byte PROCMAP_QUERY at SQLite’s actual page-zero address, checking range, zero offset, shared/readable permissions and device/inode. The syscall uses the kernel VMA lookup; the host does not parse the mapping list.",
    "cached": "Full address-specific mapping check once in the initial read transaction. During that same call the live open generation, native mapping generation, pointer and size must continue matching, in addition to FILESTAT, descriptor, name, and lock checks."
  },
